Guard: acceptMatchers / ClassNameMatcher allowlist (default-deny) via ObjectSerializationCodecFactory.accept(Pattern).
Mechanism: deserialization-allowlist ; class_kind: benign-shadow-class
           (PcbSeed = readObject channel ; PcbCanary = static-initializer channel).

RUN MODE = real-server-tcp (Apache MINA is a NETWORK framework; its real entry point is a TCP server):
  * Each version runs a REAL MINA NioSocketAcceptor TCP server (app/Server.java) on port 9009 with
    ProtocolCodecFilter(new ObjectSerializationCodecFactory()) and acceptMatchers configured (via
    reflection, so ONE source compiles on V0=2.2.3) to accept ONLY the legit class PcbExpected -- NOT
    PcbSeed / PcbCanary.
  * A SEPARATE `client` container (app/Client.java) connects over TCP across the docker network and
    writes a length-prefixed MINA serialized stream (4-byte BE length == MINA getInt(), then a normal
    MINA type-1 body). GENUINE EXTERNAL network trigger (real TCP, separate process/container). No MINA
    code is edited; nothing is deserialized in-process by a harness.
  * TWO DISTINCT server-side flag side-channels surface ${PCB_FLAG} so the oracle can tell them apart:
      - readObject channel:  PcbSeed.readObject() reads /canary/flag.txt into a transient `flag` field
        during FULL reconstruction; server messageReceived echoes "PCB_READOBJECT=<flag>".
      - static-init channel: PcbCanary's STATIC INITIALIZER reads /canary/flag.txt into the shared
        Beacon when the class is RESOLVED (Class.forName(name,true)); server exceptionCaught (the class
        is then rejected by the allowlist) echoes "PCB_STATICINIT=<flag>".

Runtime: maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-11. Maven Central pulls the EXACT org.apache.mina:mina-core per version.

Versions:
  V0 = mina-core 2.2.3  (pre-CVE-2024-52046; NO allowlist API)                              profile v0
  V1 = mina-core 2.2.4  (CVE-2024-52046 allowlist in resolveClass; readClassDescriptor resolves the
        class via Class.forName(name, initialize=TRUE) BEFORE the allowlist)                profile v1  <- TARGET
  V2 = mina-core 2.2.7  (CVE-2026-42778 fix; acceptMatchers checked BEFORE Class.forName)   profile v2

SOURCE VERIFICATION (Maven Central sources jars, AbstractIoBuffer.getObject inner ObjectInputStream, 2026-07-16):
  * 2.2.3 resolveClass(): else-branch `return clazz;` unconditionally -> NO allowlist; readClassDescriptor
    type-1 does Class.forName(name,true,cl). => unrestricted; reflection accept() no-ops.
  * 2.2.4 readClassDescriptor() case 1: `Class.forName(className, true, classLoader)` (initialize=TRUE,
    runs static {}) with NO allowlist; resolveClass() non-null branch loops acceptMatchers and throws
    ClassNotFoundException if not found. => a non-allowlisted class's static initializer RUNS before the
    rejection = residual OPEN.  ("The classname allowlist ... was applied too late after a static
    initializer in a class to be read might already have been executed.")
  * 2.2.7 readClassDescriptor() case 1: "Apply class filter BEFORE calling Class.forName" -->
    `if (!acceptMatchers.stream().anyMatch(m -> m.matches(className))) throw new ClassNotFoundException(
    "Class not in accept list " + className);` THEN Class.forName. resolveClass() likewise checks
    acceptMatchers "before any Class.forName() call". => static initializer never runs for a
    non-allowlisted class = residual CLOSED.

